      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 99,
      "outputTokens": 739,
      "costUsd": 0.0067005,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the period. We assume the tide follows a smooth cos-shaped wave, and that these are consecutive tides, so high to low is only half a cycle, and a full cycle, high back to high, takes twelve hours. For one cycle, the inside, a times t, has to grow by two pi. So ay is two pi divided by twelve, which is pi over six. That's the period rule, read backwards: ay equals two pi over the period."
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-04",
      "changed": true,
      "audio": "public/audio/math-a12-t03/scene-04.wav",
      "durationInFrames": 1078,
      "worstWordGap": {
