      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 112,
      "outputTokens": 898,
      "costUsd": 0.008138000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Which curve should we use? At time zero the water is at its highest, and the cos curve starts at its peak. So no slide is needed: h equals three cos of pi t over six, plus four point five. Check the other measurement. At t equals six, the inside is pi, cos pi is minus one, and h is minus three plus four point five: one point five, low tide. A sine model works too, with plus pi over two inside, which slides it left by three hours, but cos is simpler here."
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-05",
      "changed": true,
      "audio": "public/audio/math-a12-t03/scene-05.wav",
