      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 85,
      "outputTokens": 621,
      "costUsd": 0.0056315,
      "pronunciationText": "Now use the model. What's the water level four hours after high tide? The inside is four pi over six, which is two pi over three. Cos of two pi over three is exactly minus a half, so h is minus one point five plus four point five: three metres. On the graph, the water is below the midline and still falling, as it should be, two hours before low tide."
    },
