      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 187,
      "outputTokens": 1443,
      "costUsd": 0.0130805,
      "pronunciationText": "Harder question: when is the water level five point two five metres, in the first twelve hours? There's one cycle, and the level is between low and high, so expect two times. Three cos of pi t over six, plus four point five, equals five point two five, so cos of pi t over six is a quarter. A quarter isn't an exact value, so use inverse cos on a calculator, in radians: pi t over six is about one point three one eight, and t is about two point five two hours. By symmetry, the other angle is two pi minus that, so t is about nine point four eight. So a boat that needs the level at least five and a quarter metres can come in for about the first two and a half hours, and again from about nine and a half hours until twelve, in this first cycle. The model repeats that every twelve hours."
    },
