      "inputTokens": 118,
      "outputTokens": 973,
      "costUsd": 0.008816,
      "pronunciationText": "Remember the Ferris wheel seat? Here's one with numbers: radius ten metres, its centre twelve metres above the ground, turning once every sixty seconds. Follow one cabin, starting at the bottom. As the wheel turns, its height traces a wave. Midline twelve, amplitude ten, and period sixty, so ay is two pi over sixty, pi over thirty. It starts at the lowest point, so we need the cos curve turned upside down: h equals twelve minus ten cos of pi t over thirty. Check: at thirty seconds, h is twenty two, the top."
    },
