      "costUsd": 0.0065095,
      "pronunciationText": "Your turn. In a coastal town, the longest day has fourteen and a half hours of daylight, and the shortest day, six months later, has nine and a half. Assume a sinusoidal pattern, with these as consecutive extremes. Let t be the number of months after the longest day, and model the daylight hours as D equals k cos a t, plus c. Find k, a and c, then find D when t equals two. Pause here to answer."
